{
    "background_story": "Promise was a bright and ambitious student from Durham, North Carolina. Growing up in a low-income household, she faced numerous challenges, but her determination to succeed never wavered. Promise worked multiple jobs while attending high school, all while maintaining a stellar academic record. Her hard work paid off when she earned a full scholarship to Duke University, one of Durham's most prestigious institutions. At Duke, Promise excelled in her studies, becoming a leader in the African American student union and a vocal advocate for social justice. After graduating, she returned to her community, founding a non-profit organization that provided educational resources and mentorship to underprivileged youth in Durham. Promise's commitment to giving back to her community earned her numerous accolades, solidifying her reputation as a beacon of hope and inspiration in Durham.",
